[38;2;138;138;138mCOMMANDS[0m
  init         Create a project — just a name, no folder.
  add          Capture a task — title plus inline sugar.
  modify       Change a task — set fields or --clear them.
  list         List tasks matching a filter.
  agenda       What is coming up, when — `list` ordered by time.
  next         The one highest-urgency unblocked task.
  dashboard    Open the overview screen, or ask for its panels as data.
  pick         Browse tasks on a full-screen list: read one, search them, start one.
  show         Show one task in full detail.
  why          Explain a task's urgency score.
  start        Mark a task active.
  stop         Pause an active task.
  done         Complete a task.
  cancel       Cancel a task.
  reopen       Reopen a completed or cancelled task.
  undo         Take back the last thing this store recorded.
  annotate     Attach a timestamped note to a task.
  unannotate   Permanently scrub one annotation's text, by id.
  tag          Attach tags to a task.
  untag        Remove tags from a task.
  dep          Make one task depend on another.
  undep        Remove a dependency edge.
  use          Set the default project for bare adds.
  archive      Retire a project — out of rotation, tasks untouched.
  projects     List projects (default marked with `*`).
  check        Acceptance criteria on a task: add, mark, drop.
  brief        Everything needed before starting a task, in one read.
  report       Summary counts, or outcomes, optionally grouped, as text or HTML.
  chart        Render throughput, heatmap, or burndown charts.
  theme        List or preview terminal themes.
  config       Read and change tasqx settings.
  memory       Store and search knowledge: docs, patterns, and your task annotations (D41).
  tokens       Repair stored token attribution — dry-run by default (D50).
  export       Dump tasks as canonical JSON.
  import       Load tasks from a JSON file or stdin.
  api          One JSON envelope in on stdin → one out on stdout.
  daemon       Long-lived single-writer server.
  watch        Live-updating task view.
  mcp          Serve MCP over stdio with an operator-selected scope.
  docs         Open the exhaustive browser guide (self-contained HTML).
  about        Who made tasqx, where to find it, and what build this is.
  manual       Browse the complete guide in your terminal.
  completions  Turn on Tab completion for your shell.

▸ Jump to a topic or command:  tasqx manual <name>
▸ Full browser guide:          tasqx docs

